{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02430",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.95,
      "end_seconds": 4.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "morning, doctor i've settled them in, ready when you are"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.36,
      "end_seconds": 9.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.24,
      "end_seconds": 16.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Well, doctor, I'm just here to to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.02,
      "end_seconds": 34.02,
      "duration_seconds": 16.0,
      "text": "I've been dealing with pain in the lower left tummy work has been very busy so so I kept ignoring it i wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.53,
      "end_seconds": 35.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.33,
      "end_seconds": 43.54,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "For about a week, I'd say. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.56,
      "end_seconds": 46.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "What brings it it on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.66,
      "end_seconds": 52.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I, I notice it more with moving."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.54,
      "end_seconds": 56.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "How much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.22,
      "end_seconds": 61.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "a seven out of ten, I suppose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.33,
      "end_seconds": 66.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.02,
      "end_seconds": 73.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a low fever as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.01,
      "end_seconds": 80.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 80.51,
      "end_seconds": 86.79,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.37,
      "end_seconds": 93.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on. Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.58,
      "end_seconds": 97.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "about a four out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.03,
      "end_seconds": 100.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "how often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.72,
      "end_seconds": 108.38,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "hmm, it's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.32,
      "end_seconds": 116.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.54,
      "end_seconds": 121.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 126.56,
      "end_seconds": 134.55,
      "duration_seconds": 7.99,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse is 102 beats a minute, saturation 98 percent, BP is 119 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.22,
      "end_seconds": 136.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.08,
      "end_seconds": 142.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.74,
      "end_seconds": 145.64,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.25,
      "end_seconds": 149.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "tell me if that's sore"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.98,
      "end_seconds": 168.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "It is tender in the lower left with no guarding or rigidity."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.36,
      "end_seconds": 179.85,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Have you had weight loss, by any chance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.92,
      "end_seconds": 189.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "not at all, um, no weight loss"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.39,
      "end_seconds": 195.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Have you had any blood in the stool, urinary symptoms or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.37,
      "end_seconds": 215.76,
      "duration_seconds": 15.39,
      "text": "no, no blood in the stool, no urinary symptoms, no vomiting. I did have constipation then loose stools at one point, but that that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.55,
      "end_seconds": 219.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.87,
      "end_seconds": 223.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.03,
      "end_seconds": 225.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.45,
      "end_seconds": 228.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.48,
      "end_seconds": 234.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.85,
      "end_seconds": 243.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.17,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a little pink tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.53,
      "end_seconds": 246.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.01,
      "end_seconds": 263.9,
      "duration_seconds": 16.89,
      "text": "let me think, for my blood pressure, I believe my son sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given i'm on alendronate, 70 milligrams, maybe, once a week for my bones"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.86,
      "end_seconds": 270.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "So, did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.53,
      "end_seconds": 280.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Well, I take naproxen, 250 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 282.32,
      "end_seconds": 289.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "It's meant to be twice a day, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.71,
      "end_seconds": 295.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "I was on lisinopril before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.56,
      "end_seconds": 300.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.84,
      "end_seconds": 313.25,
      "duration_seconds": 11.41,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure i, I have thin bones, for about a year. Arthritis in my knees, for about ten years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.0,
      "end_seconds": 327.21,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high blood pressure and thin bones in your file as well. Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.61,
      "end_seconds": 332.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Tramadol. I come out in... well, vomiting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.93,
      "end_seconds": 344.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.56,
      "end_seconds": 359.74,
      "duration_seconds": 13.18,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I grab fast food at lunch most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.86,
      "end_seconds": 371.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.06,
      "end_seconds": 378.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "Hmm, I had my womb taken out fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.53,
      "end_seconds": 390.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.71,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with acute diverticulitis. It could also be a bowel tumour, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 392.04,
      "end_seconds": 396.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "I'm, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.03,
      "end_seconds": 413.45,
      "duration_seconds": 15.42,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's acute diverticulitis, and we'll know more once the a CT scan is back. a CT scan is what I'd like next, for left iliac fossa pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 414.6,
      "end_seconds": 418.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I can book that for Thursday at 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.28,
      "end_seconds": 434.85,
      "duration_seconds": 14.57,
      "text": "I'll request blood tests, it'll help with abdominal pain. Let's use co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, five days. You take it by mouth. That should help with diverticulitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.37,
      "end_seconds": 438.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "Should I take that with food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 439.89,
      "end_seconds": 463.12,
      "duration_seconds": 23.23,
      "text": "drink plenty and start with a light diet and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose one warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse in that case don't wait let's plan a check in one week does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 464.56,
      "end_seconds": 467.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 469.86,
      "end_seconds": 471.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "So, take care now."
    }
  ]
}